        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "df4d045b-6206-5ac6-a51d-2ca6dcccc498",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Hodge, Danny Boyle, Irvine Welsh, Alex Garland\n- Works: Trainspotting, T2 Trainspotting, Skagboys, Porno, The Beach, Shallow Grave, A Life Less Ordinary, The Final Curtain, Alien Love Triangle\n- Roles: screenwriter, dramatist, director, novelist\n\nFacts:\n- John Hodge, born in 1964, is a British screenwriter and dramatist.\n- In 1994, John Hodge wrote the film Shallow Grave.\n- In 1996, John Hodge was most noted for adapting Irvine Welsh's novel Trainspotting into the screenplay for the film Trainspotting.\n- In 1997, John Hodge wrote the film A Life Less Ordinary.\n- In 2000, The Beach was released as a British-American adventure drama film directed by Danny Boyle and adapted for film by John Hodge from Alex Garland's 1996 novel The Beach.\n- In 2002, John Hodge wrote The Final Curtain and the short film Alien Love Triangle.\n- Porno, published in 2002, is a sequel to Irvine Welsh's 1993 novel Trainspotting.\n- Skagboys is a prequel to Irvine Welsh's 1993 novel Trainspotting and to its 2002 sequel Porno.\n- T2 Trainspotting was directed by Danny Boyle and written by John Hodge, based on characters created by Irvine Welsh in the novels Trainspotting and Porno.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "2d7f1ce4-8224-51e0-9fa2-c013f12d4caa",
        "text": "Page: John Hodge (screenwriter). Sentence: John Hodge (born 1964) is a British screenwriter and dramatist, most noted for his adaptation of Irvine Welsh's novel \"Trainspotting\" into the script for the film of the same title.\nPage: John Hodge (screenwriter). Sentence: His films include \"Shallow Grave\" (1994), \"Trainspotting\" (1996) \"A Life Less Ordinary\" (1997), \"The Beach\" (2000), \"The Final Curtain\" (2002), and the short film \"Alien Love Triangle\" (2002).\nPage: The Beach (film). Sentence: The Beach is a 2000 British-American adventure drama film directed by Danny Boyle and based on the 1996 novel of the same name by Alex Garland, which was adapted for the film by John Hodge.\nPage: T2 Trainspotting. Sentence: The film is directed by Danny Boyle and written by John Hodge, based on characters created by Irvine Welsh in his novel \"Trainspotting\" and its follow-up \"Porno\".\nPage: Skagboys. Sentence: It is a prequel to his 1993 novel \"Trainspotting\", and its 2002 sequel \"Porno\".",
